# Upstream files this branch deliberately does not carry. sync.sh reports anything new that is NOT
# matched here, so keeping this list current is what keeps that report worth reading.
#
# Shell globs, matched against the published path (unity/... or animation-agent/...).

# The 3D assets themselves are absent, so their sidecar .meta files are too.
unity/Assets/**/*.fbx.meta
unity/Assets/**/*.mesh.meta
unity/Assets/**/*.mat
unity/Assets/**/*.mat.meta

# Baked lighting and package art. The KB render frames under
# unity/agent/animation_knowledge_base/frames ARE published; these are the ones that are megabytes of
# scene bake, not evidence.
unity/Assets/Scenes/**/*.png
unity/Assets/Scenes/**/*.exr
unity/Packages/**/*.png

# The pose dumps behind the Mixamo corpus. The 2446 corpus records themselves are published; only
# these per-frame samples are not, and the working repository does not track them either. See README.md.
unity/agent/animation_knowledge_base/raw/mx_*.json

# ...and those clips' render frames, by the same rule: 2446 rings of 24 JPEG come to about 3.4 GB,
# they are regenerable offline from the dumps (`ingest_corpus.py render`), and the working repository
# does not track them either. The eight nursing actions' frames ARE published, as noted above.
unity/agent/animation_knowledge_base/frames/mx_*

# The Unity repository's own .gitattributes is where the LFS filters are declared. Publishing it
# would hand a fresh clone LFS patterns with no objects behind them.
unity/.gitattributes

# A superseded scene kept upstream as a backup.
unity/EmergencyRoom.P3backup.unity
